## Step 1: Install HAProxy (on BOTH nodes)

Per Ubuntu/Debian
#######################################
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y haproxy keepalived
#######################################

Consentire binding IP:
#######################################
echo "net.ipv4.ip_nonlocal_bind=1" | sudo tee -a /etc/sysctl.conf
sudo sysctl -p
#######################################


Configurare Keepalived
HA-PROXY01 (MASTER)
sudo vi /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf
#######################################
vrrp_script check_haproxy {
# -f: fallisce se la risposta è un errore (es. 500)
    # -s: silenzioso
    # --max-time: timeout totale (se non risponde entro 3s, è considerato morto)
    # --retry: riprova 0 volte (vogliamo un responso immediato)
    script "/usr/bin/curl -f -s --max-time 3 http://127.0.0.1:10242/healthz"

    interval 3          # Esegui il check ogni 3 secondi
    timeout 5           # Se lo script impiega più di 5s a chiudersi, fallisce
    rise 2              # Servono 2 check positivi per dichiararlo UP
    fall 3              # Servono 3 check negativi per dichiararlo DOWN (evita micro-interruzioni)
    weight 2            # Se il check passa, aumenta la priorità di 2
}

vrrp_instance VI_1 {
    state MASTER
    interface ens33             # Sostituisci con il nome della tua interfaccia (es. ens18 o enp0s3)
    virtual_router_id 51
    priority 101                # Priorità più alta per il Master
    advert_int 1
    notify_fault "/usr/bin/logger HAProxy health check failed, moving VIP"

    authentication {
        auth_type PASS
        auth_pass HA-PROXY-2026    # Usa una password uguale su entrambi i nodi
    }

    virtual_ipaddress {
        192.168.73.10/24          # Il tuo VIP
    }

    track_script {
        check_haproxy
    }
}
#######################################




HA-PROXY02 (SLAVE)
sudo nano /etc/keepalived/keepalived.conf
#######################################
vrrp_script check_haproxy {
# -f: fallisce se la risposta è un errore (es. 500)
    # -s: silenzioso
    # --max-time: timeout totale (se non risponde entro 3s, è considerato morto)
    # --retry: riprova 0 volte (vogliamo un responso immediato)
    script "/usr/bin/curl -f -s --max-time 3 http://127.0.0.1:10242/healthz"

    interval 3          # Esegui il check ogni 3 secondi
    timeout 5           # Se lo script impiega più di 5s a chiudersi, fallisce
    rise 2              # Servono 2 check positivi per dichiararlo UP
    fall 3              # Servono 3 check negativi per dichiararlo DOWN (evita micro-interruzioni)
    weight 2            # Se il check passa, aumenta la priorità di 2
}

vrrp_instance VI_1 {
    state BACKUP
    interface ens33              # Stessa interfaccia del Master
    virtual_router_id 51
    priority 100                # Priorità più bassa
    advert_int 1
    notify_fault "/usr/bin/logger HAProxy health check failed, moving VIP"

    authentication {
        auth_type PASS
        auth_pass HA-PROXY-2026
    }

    virtual_ipaddress {
        192.168.73.10/24
    }

    track_script {
        check_haproxy
    }
}
#######################################



Configurare HAProxy (`/etc/haproxy/haproxy.cfg` su ENTRAMBI I NODI)
Prima di modificare il file, fare una copia:

#######################################
sudo cp /etc/haproxy/haproxy.cfg /etc/haproxy/haproxy.cfg_old
sudo vi /etc/haproxy/haproxy.cfg
modificare in:
--------------------------------------------------------
global
    log /dev/log local0 warning
    chroot /var/lib/haproxy
    pidfile /var/run/haproxy.pid
    maxconn 4000
    user haproxy
    group haproxy
    daemon
    stats socket /var/lib/haproxy/stats

defaults
    log global
    mode tcp
    option tcplog
    option dontlognull
    timeout connect 5000
    timeout client 50000
    timeout server 50000

# Endpoint per il check di Keepalived
frontend health_check
    bind 127.0.0.1:10242        # Porta locale dedicata ai check
    mode http
    monitor-uri /healthz        # Risponderà 200 OK se il processo è reattivo


frontend microk8s-controlplane
    bind 192.168.73.10:6443		# Ascolta sul VIP porta di default di API-SERVER 6443
    mode tcp
    option tcplog
    default_backend kube-apiserver

backend kube-apiserver
    mode tcp
    option tcplog
    option tcp-check
    balance roundrobin
    default-server inter 10s downinter 5s rise 2 fall 2 slowstart 60s maxconn 250 maxqueue 256 weight 100
    # Sostituisci con l'IP dei nodi MASTER
    server k8s-m01 192.168.73.21:6443 check
    server k8s-m02 192.168.73.22:6443 check
    server k8s-m03 192.168.73.23:6443 check

----------------------------------------------------
#######################################



Start HAProxy e Keepalived:
#######################################
sudo systemctl restart haproxy 
sudo systemctl restart keepalived
#######################################

Per monitorare gli errori di keepalived:
journalctl -u keepalived -f




## Step 4: Firewall Configuration (Critical!)

Allow VRRP traffic and service ports on BOTH nodes:

 Ubuntu/Debian (ufw)
sudo ufw allow proto vrrp
sudo ufw allow 16443/tcp


Se il commando “ Sudo ufw allow proto vrrp” non funziona: 
###############################################
# Stop and disable UFW
sudo ufw disable
sudo systemctl disable ufw

# Apply iptables rules (as shown above)
sudo iptables -I INPUT -p 112 -j ACCEPT
sudo iptables -I OUTPUT -p 112 -j ACCEPT
sudo iptables -I INPUT -p tcp --dport 6443 -j ACCEPT

# Make persistent
sudo apt install -y iptables-persistent
sudo netfilter-persistent save

Verifica:
sudo iptables -L INPUT -n | grep 112

## Step 5: Verification

1. **Check VIP assignment** (on MASTER):
   ##################################################
   ip addr show | grep 10.10.148.2
   ##################################################

2. **Test failover**:
   ##################################################
   # On MASTER node:
   sudo systemctl stop keepalived
   # Then check BACKUP node:
   ip addr show | grep 10.10.148.2
   ##################################################

3. **Test API access via VIP**:
   ##################################################
   curl -k https://10.10.148.2:6443/healthz
   # Expected: "Unauthorized" (HTTP 401) = connection successful
   ##################################################

4. **Monitor Keepalived state**:
 ##################################################
   sudo journalctl -u keepalived -f
 ##################################################
